2,"text":"absolute-error maps","tone":"b"},{"x":0.78,"y":0.82,"text":"one shared colour scale","tone":"c"}]}},{"id":"b07-cnn-results","intent":"DQ-CTM-SR is competitive with the listed CNN baselines on average benchmark score.","inside":null,"claim":"Competitive with CNN baselines; behind recent lightweight transformers.","evidence":[{"kind":"section","id":"sec3"},{"kind":"table","id":"tbl-bench"}],"narration":"The average scores put DQ-CTM-SR in the same narrow band as the CNN baselines. CARN reports an average of 28.970. IMDN reports 28.968. RFDN reports 29.022. DQ-CTM-SR reports 28.983, which is close to those CNN results.","weight":0.82,"seconds":10,"archetype":"bar-compare","params":{"eyebrow":"Table 1","headline":"DQ-CTM-SR is close to the CNN baselines","unit":"Average over five benchmarks","bars":[{"label":"IMDN","value":28.968,"tone":"a"},{"label":"CARN","value":28.97,"tone":"a"},{"label":"DQ-CTM-SR","value":28.983,"tone":"c"},{"label":"RFDN","value":29.022,"tone":"a"}],"note":"Average is reported for x4 lightweight super-resolution."}},{"id":"b08-transformer-gap","intent":"The reported average leaves DQ-CTM-SR behind the recent lightweight transformer baseline CATANet.","inside":null,"claim":"Competitive with CNN baselines; behind recent lightweight transformers.","evidence":[{"kind":"section","id":"sec3"},{"kind":"table","id":"tbl-bench"}],"narration":"The same benchmark table also shows the main reported gap. DQ-CTM-SR reports an average of 28.983. CATANet reports 29.482. That makes CATANet the stronger result among the listed methods.","weight":0.84,"seconds":8,"archetype":"bar-compare","params":{"eyebrow":"Table 1","headline":"DQ-CTM-SR trails CATANet on average score","unit":"Average over five benchmarks","bars":[{"label":"DQ-CTM-SR","value":28.983,"tone":"c"},{"label":"CATANet","value":29.482,"tone":"d"}],"note":"CATANet is the recent lightweight transformer baseline in the table."}},{"id":"b09-parameter-cost","intent":"DQ-CTM-SR is not the smallest model among the reported lightweight methods.","inside":null,"claim":"Table 1 — x4 lightweight super-resolution, average over five benchmarks.","evidence":[{"kind":"table","id":"tbl-bench"}],"narration":"The parameter counts show that compact thought does not make this version the smallest model in the table. CATANet reports 0.535 million parameters. RFDN reports 0.550 million parameters. DQ-CTM-SR reports 1.129 million parameters. CARN remains the largest listed model at 1.592 million parameters.","weight":0.62,"seconds":10,"archetype":"bar-compare","params":{"eyebrow":"Table 1","headline":"DQ-CTM-SR is mid-sized among the listed models","unit":"million parameters","bars":[{"label":"CATANet","value":0.535,"tone":"d"},{"label":"RFDN","value":0.55,"tone":"a"},{"label":"IMDN","value":0.715,"tone":"a"},{"label":"DQ-CTM-SR","value":1.129,"tone":"c"},{"label":"CARN","value":1.592,"tone":"a"}],"note":"Params are reported in millions."}},{"id":"b10-takeaway","intent":"ThinkSR's contribution is the persistent dense carrier updated by compact thought, with results close to CNNs but below CATANet.","inside":null,"claim":"A persistent dense carrier, read and updated by a compact thought process.","evidence":[{"kind":"section","id":"sec2"},{"kind":"section","id":"sec3"}],"narration":"The source's central idea is not that compact thought replaces spatial structure. It is that a dense carrier stays present while compact thought reads and updates it. The reported outcome is competitive with CNN baselines. The stated limitation is that recent lightweight transformers remain ahead.","weight":0.9,"seconds":9,"archetype":"callout","params":{"eyebrow":"Takeaway","headline":"ThinkSR keeps density outside the compact thought state","panels":[{"label":"Method","lines":["persistent dense carrier","compact read-update process"]},{"label":"Reported result","lines":["competitive with CNN baselines","behind recent lightweight transformers"]}],"note":null}}]}
